# I added a specific template for micro posts!
Heya everyone! I've been meaning to make more frequent and small posts, but I've felt bad making low effort posts while using the picture frame blog icons. It feels like if I'm going to put a blog post in a unique frame, it had better be good. So I've made a new one styled like a tearaway daily calendar for my smaller "microblog" posts! Check it out:
![Blog icon image for this post](/resources/blog/tearaway_example.png)

I'm glad I found the handwriting font that I used for the bottom, I think it's pretty cool! The author of the font said it's a tracing of John Frusciante's handwriting. Apparently he's a famous guitarist? I wonder what inspired the author to make his handwriting into a font, and I wonder how he got writing samples from him? It's a mystery to me...

I learned about the idea of microblogging from [luvstarkei's site](https://luvstarkei.com/), and I've been wanting to do it for a while ever since they started. And I got the idea to make the graphic a tear away calendar because of this cool bird calendar my partner got me for Christmas!
![Bird themed tearaway calendar, displaying a loon](/resources/blog/irl_tearaway.jpg)
*Today happens to be the common loon, which is the bird of my home state (Minnesota)*

Anyway, I should get some sleep now. I've stayed up too late getting this new tearaway calendar thing working. See you all later!